[39m←  ☒ Redaction [38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Usernames [39m[49m ✔ Submit  →

[1m[38;5;231mHow should usernames be logged?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mFull in Node, hashed in browser (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mKeeps correlation power where logs stay local; limits PII exposure on the sink that may leave the device. Requires
[39m     [38;5;246ma small stable-hash helper.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Always full
     [38;5;246mMaximum debuggability — a production report maps straight to log lines. Puts identifiable PII into anything the [39m
     [38;5;246mbrowser sink later ships.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Always hashed
     [38;5;246mConsistent behavior in both halves, correlation still works across entries. You lose the ability to look up 'what [39m
     [38;5;246mhappened to this specific user' without hashing their name first.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
[38;5;246m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
